# Exclude non-app files from the static-assets bundle (honored by wrangler
# for both `wrangler dev` and `wrangler deploy`). Without this, the .git
# directory's large objects (28 MiB pack) blow past the 25 MiB per-asset
# limit and the Worker refuses to boot (verified locally: `wrangler dev`
# failed with "Asset too large." pointing at .git/objects/...).
# NOTE: everything the APP serves at runtime stays included — js/, css/,
# vendor/whisper (offline transcription), manifests, icons, and pages.
#
# Parity with the deploy script: real deploy excludes *.md and *.json then
# copies package.json + wrangler.jsonc back. We mirror that here so CI's
# dry-run validates the same asset bundle that ships to production.
.git
.wrangler
node_modules
.dev.vars
serve.cjs
qa-*.cjs
tools
migrations
*.md
*.json
!package.json
!wrangler.jsonc
!skills-lock.json
